# Keep the Docker build context small and free of host build artifacts.
# Used by client/catapult/Dockerfile.selfcontained (context = repository root).

.git
**/.git

# catapult local build / dependency output (generated by Dockerfile or manual builds)
client/catapult/_build
client/catapult/_deps
client/catapult/build

# node / js artifacts
**/node_modules
**/.yarn
**/dist
**/coverage

# python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# editor / OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# --- cache stability -----------------------------------------------------------
# `COPY client/catapult /src/client/catapult` sits ABOVE the ~50 minute cmake/ninja
# layer, so its cache key — the content hash of that directory — decides whether a
# rebuild recompiles catapult. Anything in there that the image does not actually need
# therefore costs an hour every time it is edited. The Dockerfile itself was the worst
# offender: editing it invalidated the compile it describes.
#
# The nemtus staging scripts live in .github/catapult/scripts for the same reason and are
# copied in their own layer below the compile; only test-only material is excluded here.
client/catapult/Dockerfile.selfcontained
